{"id": "clm:035caf9f66fde59760e897b9f89f2166afcd97b7000739439eca5b30f7ae661b", "type": "statement", "text": "`find_one()` returns the first matching document as a Python dictionary, or `None` when no document matches. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/languages/python/pymongo-driver/current/crud/query/find.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PyMongo CRUD API, cursors and bulk_write"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pymongo.readthedocs.io/en/stable/api/pymongo/collection.html"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f112603bfac7ba584d3d09316d301fc1168aed1ca9ab45f409d34cf32cab478b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:407090d0923f46397d9816950b174fa68e97f7879dcb24688c61b5fe2ef6ea45"]}
{"id": "clm:b3a389ae4e5d902705fe5091f563b4d84ec3ba597de4f04a88aa9c7880512518", "type": "statement", "text": "Call `close()` when abandoning a cursor early, or use `with collection.find() as cursor:` so the cursor closes when the block ends. Exhausted ordinary cursors close automatically. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/languages/python/pymongo-driver/current/crud/query/cursors.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PyMongo CRUD API, cursors and bulk_write"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pymongo.readthedocs.io/en/stable/api/pymongo/collection.html"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f112603bfac7ba584d3d09316d301fc1168aed1ca9ab45f409d34cf32cab478b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:7d8f197c6529a4f318a094a0ac69900273c04d9712fa9d49af020581c61cbd45", "ev:825e3d2361a23638d368ebe97bc46929ec03621e725c0bb2cede9ef786fc238c"]}
{"id": "clm:b7c1063d3a2aee0fc209f8c1a3122428c397bfe5393f61fc25aa4f54ee3bb14d", "type": "statement", "text": "Client-level operation models need a namespace: the `InsertOne` implementation rejects a missing namespace when adding an operation to a client bulk. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/mongo-python-driver/blob/main/pymongo/operations.py", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PyMongo CRUD API, cursors and bulk_write"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f112603bfac7ba584d3d09316d301fc1168aed1ca9ab45f409d34cf32cab478b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2a0665a0c03a737702e1b0afec7dd73fbcb5937190d00df4eb98f11481f9beea"]}
{"id": "clm:d685f459f885e8fd26fbf687b3f084a3d82c981bed6cd477dd8c770addd358bf", "type": "statement", "text": "Cursors return read results in iterable batches and hold a subset of the documents in memory; this supports processing large results incrementally. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/languages/python/pymongo-driver/current/crud/query/cursors.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PyMongo CRUD API, cursors and bulk_write"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/languages/python/pymongo-driver/current/crud/query/find.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f112603bfac7ba584d3d09316d301fc1168aed1ca9ab45f409d34cf32cab478b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:6ffe83bd7d76a0a2636e783e5da6216ad3d367a17bdb92e96a49b6d4c4a24910", "ev:c117de593f4289f2c8d36f82f8cc04c75218827fb0e7d6155999ad237e9588d9"]}
{"id": "clm:a8ce79400dd21647815afe172ee0e3f34878975484b2322d23dd2ea356ba9103", "type": "statement", "text": "Use `insert_one()` for one document and `insert_many()` for a list of documents. The driver generates an `ObjectId` for a missing `_id`; explicitly supplied `_id` values must be unique within the collection. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/languages/python/pymongo-driver/current/crud/insert.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PyMongo CRUD API, cursors and bulk_write"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "how-to", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/languages/python/pymongo-driver/current/crud.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f112603bfac7ba584d3d09316d301fc1168aed1ca9ab45f409d34cf32cab478b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:05105fac9486b21d6d071b40a81dceed96735041e448644956501ed3077b4576", "ev:95911d3bdf1c6fa442a8335bfe8152e3c06ad170b05cabc8f59e9070e71a154e"]}
{"id": "clm:1c284ce2be1a86b39b0b8a29aac7ddf27f3e5838634175a81ee7b4037deedfbf", "type": "statement", "text": "Use `limit()`, `sort()`, and `skip()` to shape query results. When combined, the driver applies sort and skip before limit regardless of the order of these method calls. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/languages/python/pymongo-driver/current/crud/query/specify-documents-to-return.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PyMongo CRUD API, cursors and bulk_write"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f112603bfac7ba584d3d09316d301fc1168aed1ca9ab45f409d34cf32cab478b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:654bb838748689100ce8911fc0c7892fb794db2ebae42ed78b82183d3eda72a6", "ev:d9f76a1fe7852ed83ba00380fde1bc172e4b96185f8dd6a956a3b7cc188aa39a"]}
{"id": "clm:dc7fc1eebcf4711e8ee6a8a1c191e415577a7870d83f066bbce12a83a0e48e90", "type": "statement", "text": "A cursor is not a Python list. Each index access or slice runs a new query using skip and limit, so iterating with repeated `cursor[idx]` accesses is inefficient and can produce surprising results. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://pymongo.readthedocs.io/en/stable/api/pymongo/cursor.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PyMongo CRUD API, cursors and bulk_write"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f112603bfac7ba584d3d09316d301fc1168aed1ca9ab45f409d34cf32cab478b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:36ee34ce6e296659007e68e43f00b8d0590e9012301c60ede918556306210a91"]}
{"id": "clm:c4814de87b049340e9981debe61726d3f9c0b65cafc1127f4dd663be3d96cab5", "type": "statement", "text": "For collection bulk writes, `ordered` defaults to `True`: the driver preserves operation order and skips remaining operations after an individual write error. With `ordered=False`, the driver attempts all individual writes in arbitrary order and reports write errors after those attempts. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/languages/python/pymongo-driver/current/crud/bulk-write.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PyMongo CRUD API, cursors and bulk_write"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/crud/bulk-write.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f112603bfac7ba584d3d09316d301fc1168aed1ca9ab45f409d34cf32cab478b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:60623b5adbfb6e3ecfdcaafb013867b3e5ea3b878f1cbe4668d67b10e65a783b", "ev:9a7f66bcffdd44f8e0dcfc4791e399b6e7fc1536f695923186869f47686e99f3", "ev:e9a0087e2b7f466c359a84bd00ee08154ce3efa98d436653019cca879a032d99"]}
{"id": "clm:d40ecf4792c93da52cd2a2ec3276d0e6c2a4cea15dda655ab7e9253bf890466e", "type": "statement", "text": "Unordered client bulk writes still stop on a top-level error such as a network or command error; continuing after an individual write error does not guarantee completion after communication failure. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/crud/bulk-write.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PyMongo CRUD API, cursors and bulk_write"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f112603bfac7ba584d3d09316d301fc1168aed1ca9ab45f409d34cf32cab478b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:37d623edb5b721b40705c8e065100726540584bbd5223cd2293b8020fef3176c", "ev:7416396a5fd221d83d1d79e8e78ee6e72533682fffcdf860c7d8e817a9eb55de"]}
{"id": "clm:fc44ed78c032ac7b989d1569efb6e1755ca4b8149cc9d9160b4a9a36778c950e", "type": "statement", "text": "Collection bulk failures use `BulkWriteError`, whose `details` includes failure information. Client bulk failures use `ClientBulkWriteException`; its `error` describes top-level failure and can be absent for individual write failures. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/languages/python/pymongo-driver/current/crud/bulk-write.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PyMongo CRUD API, cursors and bulk_write"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/mongo-python-driver/blob/main/pymongo/errors.py"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f112603bfac7ba584d3d09316d301fc1168aed1ca9ab45f409d34cf32cab478b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:517eaf6d136a40873ce2f9395fc6ab5e2c46dfdccb3bd7a7d0de90495589b87c", "ev:749a53249111f88fe2dc8703d66c1452798a1591c12bbec1afcb763c4141e4ae"]}
{"id": "clm:7e1d032d9e36a36babefe01c5c33319ba5d593a922cb54527c410a5b3d47db6e", "type": "statement", "text": "A client bulk exception can expose `partial_result`, containing successful operations performed before the error. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/mongo-python-driver/blob/main/pymongo/errors.py", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PyMongo CRUD API, cursors and bulk_write"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f112603bfac7ba584d3d09316d301fc1168aed1ca9ab45f409d34cf32cab478b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:3564e334b3001945bd961b4898f88b1618b2c69a46c10c3787c688806f761fb6"]}
{"id": "clm:0160f2c62e29d2077d13efa0c9f28efcbf07f57c5e24569f8e574929f7a1ad2d", "type": "statement", "text": "Collection `bulk_write()` defaults to `ordered=True`: requests execute serially in the provided order, and a write error aborts remaining operations. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/languages/python/pymongo-driver/current/crud/bulk-write.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PyMongo CRUD API, cursors and bulk_write"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pymongo.readthedocs.io/en/stable/api/pymongo/collection.html"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f112603bfac7ba584d3d09316d301fc1168aed1ca9ab45f409d34cf32cab478b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:bedae90fae7c589e91ce00ea7e28c90380e427ad5a85f1c7d203af93aa0ef05f", "ev:bf76797a44c69d05df519c9ff53449dd19c15d57b259a3c7b32105d629c303c4"]}
{"id": "clm:60b9f5e8a86385ac5dcf0a52c9e42521ad12a4e02b625037fda2bbd619b92eb4", "type": "statement", "text": "The bulk-write guide’s introductory failure paragraph says a collection write failure stops further operations. Its unordered section and the collection API qualify this: unordered bulk writes attempt all operations. Read the introductory stop statement in the context of ordered execution. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/languages/python/pymongo-driver/current/crud/bulk-write.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PyMongo CRUD API, cursors and bulk_write"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pymongo.readthedocs.io/en/stable/api/pymongo/collection.html"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f112603bfac7ba584d3d09316d301fc1168aed1ca9ab45f409d34cf32cab478b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:1e41aefb8d3245fc4143b685aacd58505c51568ab5f7a6c3d6b4e48a0a9bf914", "ev:2606950abf5e8ab3ae2ad0e32befbe757e5f8dea44bcf6070c482dc69bd35b82", "ev:60623b5adbfb6e3ecfdcaafb013867b3e5ea3b878f1cbe4668d67b10e65a783b"]}
{"id": "clm:88ce95279d7eb24293ff2cedda97fc449501938c0b78a8687bdf79b449ae47f5", "type": "statement", "text": "`find()` returns matching documents through a cursor; iterate it with a `for` loop so the application can process results in batches rather than retain the complete result set. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/languages/python/pymongo-driver/current/crud/query/find.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PyMongo CRUD API, cursors and bulk_write"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/languages/python/pymongo-driver/current/crud/query/cursors.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f112603bfac7ba584d3d09316d301fc1168aed1ca9ab45f409d34cf32cab478b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:a75a5ccfa6a435063507797392f41743b33525c32928eea0a617094e2f516b1a", "ev:c117de593f4289f2c8d36f82f8cc04c75218827fb0e7d6155999ad237e9588d9"]}
{"id": "clm:47878298272a55d2b21f5715edacff4b8dcb0d95d88c348ae70c6a9220536c78", "type": "statement", "text": "`find()` accepts a query filter and returns a cursor; an empty filter selects all documents. Iterate the cursor with a `for` loop instead of materializing the entire result. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/languages/python/pymongo-driver/current/crud/query/find.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PyMongo CRUD API, cursors and bulk_write"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pymongo.readthedocs.io/en/stable/api/pymongo/collection.html"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f112603bfac7ba584d3d09316d301fc1168aed1ca9ab45f409d34cf32cab478b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:7fc26e8a7d1c114b236fe5797a1269515da862c293b2a23e3c8b415e1562e87a", "ev:9ce8a64c95cf6056b5ca5593aa716edf0f293ac1a22e2b51645a018630f61ce9"]}
{"id": "clm:71bc72da656713dc9af335a933bab85c554aff88308844bf4bc3e685ff109998", "type": "statement", "text": "The synchronous CRUD examples use `update_one()` or `update_many()` with a query filter and a `$set` update document, `replace_one()` with a replacement document, and `delete_one()` or `delete_many()` with a query filter. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/languages/python/pymongo-driver/current/crud.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PyMongo CRUD API, cursors and bulk_write"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f112603bfac7ba584d3d09316d301fc1168aed1ca9ab45f409d34cf32cab478b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:e6e4ad5efe8f6dbe2eee27df234f287142c9d7852be38488b7087f5753f77798"]}
{"id": "clm:663f86954ac9e4b82d313fb9b9fc9b7bcd82585ac268728db1f5c4fa5fac1356", "type": "statement", "text": "Converting a cursor with `list(results)` retrieves all its documents into application memory. The cursor guide warns that results exceeding available memory can crash the program and recommends iterative access for large results. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/languages/python/pymongo-driver/current/crud/query/cursors.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PyMongo CRUD API, cursors and bulk_write"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f112603bfac7ba584d3d09316d301fc1168aed1ca9ab45f409d34cf32cab478b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:40e5169e6c6aaa4a2456d087b617d389ec9597cf704248d12c18e40939599d26"]}
{"id": "clm:2b2605a9bf1c36123553ef5d3446ead8d791dbf429ef274c7e95f7d93b84abd5", "type": "statement", "text": "The documented minimums for `MongoClient` bulk operations are PyMongo v4.9 and MongoDB Server v8.0. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/languages/python/pymongo-driver/current/crud/bulk-write.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PyMongo CRUD API, cursors and bulk_write"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f112603bfac7ba584d3d09316d301fc1168aed1ca9ab45f409d34cf32cab478b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:32451370538d285448e2daccbe7b3df571b9ae0f748117e78d00fac355016c64"]}
{"id": "clm:fef272032e0eb45a5278c17dc5f672fb92789a2108ba8438c2ffa0cd36058094", "type": "statement", "text": "`Collection.bulk_write()` returns `BulkWriteResult`, with inserted, deleted, matched, modified and upserted counts; `upserted_ids` maps operation indexes to the inserted `_id` values. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/languages/python/pymongo-driver/current/crud/bulk-write.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PyMongo CRUD API, cursors and bulk_write"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pymongo.readthedocs.io/en/stable/api/pymongo/collection.html"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f112603bfac7ba584d3d09316d301fc1168aed1ca9ab45f409d34cf32cab478b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:3e9548f102abfb7d7f136b1dd56b7b2f9b12f65e77adecd5aad901f57ce87e09", "ev:be45a6d63b21c60f160615231d3c441d9c6f3af0b44a39d143726e20c21afb3e"]}
{"id": "clm:13b80485fec6ae59d5b5f8947047d121d4538f1828fd4a5917a26e6e42b88f7d", "type": "statement", "text": "The driver bulk-write specification records write-concern errors without terminating bulk execution solely for that reason, then requires an exception at the end if any occurred. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/crud/bulk-write.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PyMongo CRUD API, cursors and bulk_write"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f112603bfac7ba584d3d09316d301fc1168aed1ca9ab45f409d34cf32cab478b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:49a8dce962cafe4db4ad656e1ed5442f6b2af2fec49c1cccc9b926123e8dccbf"]}
{"id": "clm:0fba5bf0db7a3b4c282cc6e3de073c1145aa393c9d58e53d549c14ac4f651b1f", "type": "statement", "text": "`projection` restricts the returned fields. In the collection API, a list projection always includes `_id`; use a mapping to exclude `_id`. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://pymongo.readthedocs.io/en/stable/api/pymongo/collection.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PyMongo CRUD API, cursors and bulk_write"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f112603bfac7ba584d3d09316d301fc1168aed1ca9ab45f409d34cf32cab478b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:4414b139af9908b185cf01d01b99b70d2ffa3edcca363f7e6913ef1dc108c76f", "ev:4c4be26c5a49611699db13e3bc86d694fa7d54aaecd853fbd71da5adadfbbe63"]}
